# Repository-wide ignores.
#
# Both projects keep their own file, and those stay authoritative for their own
# build output: `enterprise-gpt-ui/.gitignore` is the Angular CLI set plus this
# project's generated assets, and `enterprise-gpt-api/.gitignore` is the standard
# Visual Studio set. Their patterns are rooted to their own directory, which is
# correct — nothing here is meant to replace them.
#
# What belongs here is the repository-level surface those two cannot see: local
# tool state beside the checked-in configuration, and the same build artefacts
# turning up anywhere other than the two project roots.

# --- Local tool state --------------------------------------------------------

# Worktrees are checkouts of this repository nested inside it, so git offers the
# whole second tree as untracked content. Ignored as a directory rather than by
# branch name, because the path is where `git worktree add` puts them and the
# names change per feature.
.claude/worktrees/

# Personal overrides layered on the checked-in .claude/settings.json.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.json

# --- Editors -----------------------------------------------------------------

# Mirrors the allow-list in the UI project's file: the three committed workspace
# files are shared configuration, everything else in here is per-developer.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/mcp.json
.vs/
.idea/
.history/
*.swp
*~

# --- Node and Angular --------------------------------------------------------
#
# Unrooted on purpose. The UI project already rooted these to itself, so these
# are the net for a tool run from the repository root or from a directory that
# does not exist yet.
node_modules/
dist/
.angular/
coverage/
# `npm run test:ci` writes the JUnit report CI uploads as an artifact.
test-results/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# --- .NET --------------------------------------------------------------------
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Tt]est[Rr]esults/
BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts/
*.user
*.suo
*.rsuser

# --- Secrets and machine-local configuration ---------------------------------
#
# The application takes its secrets from Key Vault through DefaultAzureCredential
# and its runtime configuration from `config.json`, so nothing below should ever
# exist in a clean checkout. They are listed because the cost of missing one is
# a committed credential.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
appsettings.*.local.json
appsettings.local.json
*.pfx
*.snk
*.p12
secrets.json

# --- Operating system --------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
